+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+<meta charset="UTF-8">
+<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
+<title>TraceLens — TODO Issues Summary · 2026-04-28</title>
+<style>
+  :root {
+    --bg: #0f1117;
+    --surface: #1a1d27;
+    --surface2: #22253a;
+    --border: #2e3250;
+    --accent: #7c6af7;
+    --accent2: #56cfb2;
+    --accent3: #f7a35c;
+    --accent4: #e05c6a;
+    --text: #e2e4f0;
+    --text-muted: #8b90b0;
+    --code-bg: #141720;
+    --tag-bug: #3d1a20;
+    --tag-bug-text: #e05c6a;
+    --tag-bug-border: #6a1f2a;
+    --tag-perf: #1a2e35;
+    --tag-perf-text: #56cfb2;
+    --tag-perf-border: #2a5048;
+    --tag-feat: #2d2260;
+    --tag-feat-text: #7c6af7;
+    --tag-feat-border: #4a3a9a;
+    --tag-doc: #2e2010;
+    --tag-doc-text: #f7a35c;
+    --tag-doc-border: #5a3a10;
+    --tag-refactor: #1e2535;
+    --tag-refactor-text: #82aaff;
+    --tag-refactor-border: #2a3a60;
+    --tag-jax: #251a35;
+    --tag-jax-text: #c792ea;
+    --tag-jax-border: #4a2a6a;
+    --pri-high: #3d1a20;
+    --pri-high-text: #e05c6a;
+    --pri-med: #2e2010;
+    --pri-med-text: #f7a35c;
+    --pri-low: #1a2a1a;
+    --pri-low-text: #56cfb2;
+  }
+  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
+  body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; }
+
+  header { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 60%, #1a1427 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 36px 48px 28px; }
+  header h1 { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); letter-spacing: -0.5px; }
+  header .meta { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 13px; margin-top: 6px; }
+  header .meta span { margin-right: 20px; }
+  header .meta strong { color: var(--text); }
+
+  .stats-bar { display: flex; gap: 16px; padding: 20px 48px; background: var(--surface); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; }
+  .stat { background: var(--surface2); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 20px; text-align: center; min-width: 100px; }
+  .stat-num { font-size: 24px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); }
+  .stat-label { font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; }
+
+  .filters { padding: 16px 48px; background: var(--surface); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; }
+  .filters label { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-right: 4px; }
+  .filter-btn { padding: 5px 14px; border-radius: 20px; border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--surface2); color: var(--text-muted); cursor: pointer; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; transition: all .15s; }
+  .filter-btn:hover, .filter-btn.active { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--text); background: #2d2260; }
+  .filter-btn.active-bug { border-color: var(--tag-bug-border); color: var(--tag-bug-text); background: var(--tag-bug); }
+  .filter-btn.active-perf { border-color: var(--tag-perf-border); color: var(--tag-perf-text); background: var(--tag-perf); }
+  .filter-btn.active-feat { border-color: var(--tag-feat-border); color: var(--tag-feat-text); background: var(--tag-feat); }
+  .filter-btn.active-doc { border-color: var(--tag-doc-border); color: var(--tag-doc-text); background: var(--tag-doc); }
+  .filter-btn.active-jax { border-color: var(--tag-jax-border); color: var(--tag-jax-text); background: var(--tag-jax); }
+
+  .table-wrapper { padding: 24px 48px 48px; overflow-x: auto; }
+  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; min-width: 1200px; }
+  thead { position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 10; }
+  th { padding: 11px 14px; text-align: left; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .8px; color: var(--text-muted); text-transform: uppercase; background: var(--surface2); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border); white-space: nowrap; }
+  td { padding: 11px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); vertical-align: top; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); }
+  tr:hover td { background: var(--surface); }
+  tr.hidden { display: none; }
+
+  td.id-cell { white-space: nowrap; }
+  td.id-cell a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-family: monospace; font-size: 12px; }
+  td.id-cell a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
+
+  td.title-cell { min-width: 220px; max-width: 280px; color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.4; }
+  td.desc-cell { min-width: 280px; max-width: 360px; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 12.5px; }
+  td.solution-cell { min-width: 240px; max-width: 320px; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 12.5px; }
+
+  .tag { display: inline-block; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 12px; margin: 2px 2px 2px 0; border: 1px solid; white-space: nowrap; }
+  .tag-bug { background: var(--tag-bug); color: var(--tag-bug-text); border-color: var(--tag-bug-border); }
+  .tag-perf { background: var(--tag-perf); color: var(--tag-perf-text); border-color: var(--tag-perf-border); }
+  .tag-feat { background: var(--tag-feat); color: var(--tag-feat-text); border-color: var(--tag-feat-border); }
+  .tag-doc { background: var(--tag-doc); color: var(--tag-doc-text); border-color: var(--tag-doc-border); }
+  .tag-refactor { background: var(--tag-refactor); color: var(--tag-refactor-text); border-color: var(--tag-refactor-border); }
+  .tag-jax { background: var(--tag-jax); color: var(--tag-jax-text); border-color: var(--tag-jax-border); }
+
+  .pri { display: inline-block; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid; white-space: nowrap; }
+  .pri-high { background: var(--pri-high); color: var(--pri-high-text); border-color: var(--tag-bug-border); }
+  .pri-med { background: var(--pri-med); color: var(--pri-med-text); border-color: var(--tag-doc-border); }
+  .pri-low { background: var(--pri-low); color: var(--pri-low-text); border-color: var(--tag-perf-border); }
+
+  .effort { display: inline-block; font-size: 10px; color: var(--text-muted); background: var(--surface2); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1px 7px; margin-left: 4px; }
+
+  code { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', 'Fira Code', monospace; font-size: 11px; background: var(--code-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 3px; padding: 1px 5px; color: var(--accent2); }
+
+  .no-results { text-align: center; padding: 60px; color: var(--text-muted); display: none; font-size: 15px; }
+</style>
+</head>
+<body>
+
+<header>
+  <h1>TraceLens — TODO Issues Summary</h1>
+  <div class="meta">
+    <span>Generated <strong>2026-04-28</strong></span>
+    <span>Source <strong>AMD-AGI/projects/37</strong></span>
+    <span>Status filter <strong>Todo</strong> (open issues)</span>
+  </div>
+</header>
+
+<div class="stats-bar">
+  <div class="stat"><div class="stat-num" id="total-count">67</div><div class="stat-label">Total TODO</div></div>
+  <div class="stat"><div class="stat-num" style="color:var(--tag-bug-text)">7</div><div class="stat-label">Bugs</div></div>
+  <div class="stat"><div class="stat-num" style="color:var(--tag-perf-text)">10</div><div class="stat-label">Perf Models</div></div>
+  <div class="stat"><div class="stat-num" style="color:var(--tag-feat-text)">18</div><div class="stat-label">Major Features</div></div>
+  <div class="stat"><div class="stat-num" style="color:var(--tag-jax-text)">8</div><div class="stat-label">JAX</div></div>
+  <div class="stat"><div class="stat-num" style="color:var(--tag-doc-text)">6</div><div class="stat-label">Docs</div></div>
+  <div class="stat"><div class="stat-num" style="color:var(--pri-high-text)">6</div><div class="stat-label">High Priority</div></div>
+</div>
+
+<div class="filters">
+  <label>Filter:</label>
+  <button class="filter-btn active" onclick="filterRows('all', this)">All</button>
+  <button class="filter-btn" onclick="filterRows('bug', this)">🐛 Bugs</button>
+  <button class="filter-btn" onclick="filterRows('perf', this)">📐 Perf Model</button>
+  <button class="filter-btn" onclick="filterRows('feat', this)">⭐ Major Feature</button>
+  <button class="filter-btn" onclick="filterRows('jax', this)">🔷 JAX</button>
+  <button class="filter-btn" onclick="filterRows('doc', this)">📄 Docs</button>
+  <button class="filter-btn" onclick="filterRows('refactor', this)">🔧 Refactor / API</button>
+  <button class="filter-btn" onclick="filterRows('high', this)">🔴 High Priority</button>
+</div>
+
+<div class="table-wrapper">
+<div class="no-results" id="no-results">No issues match the selected filter.</div>
+<table id="issues-table">
+<thead>
+  <tr>
+    <th>#</th>
+    <th>Title</th>
+    <th>What Needs to Be Done</th>
+    <th>Priority</th>
+    <th>Type</th>
+    <th>Potential Solution / Affected Files</th>
+  </tr>
+</thead>
+<tbody>
+
+<tr data-tags="feat high">
+  <td class="id-cell"><a href="https://github.com/AMD-AGI/TraceLens/issues/17" target="_blank">#17</a></td>
+  <td class="title-cell">Easy to use API for distributed performance</td>
+  <td class="desc-cell">Users currently loop manually over per-rank files and analyse separately. Need a unified API that internally loops over rank profiles, computes per-rank perf metrics, and surfaces min/max/diff across ranks. Also merge <code>NcclAnalyser</code> into this API instead of keeping it as a separate tool.</td>
+  <td><span class="pri pri-high">High</span> <span class="effort">M</span></td>
+  <td><span class="tag tag-feat">Feature</span></td>
+  <td class="solution-cell">Add a <code>DistributedPerfAnalyzer</code> wrapper in <code>TreePerf/</code> that accepts a list of trace paths, internally instantiates <code>TreePerfAnalyzer</code> per rank, aggregates DataFrames, and exposes rank-diff statistics. Integrate <code>NcclAnalyser</code> as a property.</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr data-tags="feat">
+  <td class="id-cell"><a href="https://github.com/AMD-AGI/TraceLens/issues/21" target="_blank">#21</a></td>
+  <td class="title-cell">Diagnose runtime bugs [medium term]</td>
+  <td class="desc-cell">Detect anomalies in CPU–GPU runtime interactions: async kernel launches that stall unexpectedly, sync events (H2D/D2H memcpy) that block the queue longer than expected, and device synchronizations that indicate hidden bottlenecks.</td>
+  <td><span class="pri pri-low">Low</span> <span class="effort">XL</span></td>
+  <td><span class="tag tag-feat">Major Feature</span></td>
+  <td class="solution-cell">New analysis module in <code>TreePerf/</code>. Walk the tree looking for <code>cudaDeviceSynchronize</code> / <code>hipDeviceSynchronize</code> events and measure the gap between CPU launch and GPU start. Flag cases where sync time is disproportionate to kernel duration.</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr data-tags="feat">
+  <td class="id-cell"><a href="https://github.com/AMD-AGI/TraceLens/issues/22" target="_blank">#22</a></td>
+  <td class="title-cell">Diagnose NCCL Anomalies</td>
+  <td class="desc-cell">NCCL collectives (all-reduce, all-gather) must finish at approximately the same time across ranks. Detect cases where end-time divergence across ranks exceeds a threshold — indicating NCCL/RCCL implementation bugs. Start times can legitimately differ; it's end-time skew that's anomalous.</td>
+  <td><span class="pri pri-low">Low</span> <span class="effort">XS</span></td>
+  <td><span class="tag tag-feat">Enhancement</span></td>
+  <td class="solution-cell">Extend <code>NcclAnalyser.build_df_nccl_implicit_sync_cat()</code> with end-time skew metric per collective instance. Add a <code>detect_nccl_anomalies(threshold_us)</code> method that flags instances where <code>max(end_time) - min(end_time) > threshold</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr data-tags="feat">
+  <td class="id-cell"><a href="https://github.com/AMD-AGI/TraceLens/issues/90" target="_blank">#90</a></td>
+  <td class="title-cell">Support analysis scoped by record_function regions</td>
+  <td class="desc-cell">PyTorch's <code>torch.autograd.profiler.record_function</code> adds named annotation events to traces. TraceLens should recognize these and allow: filtering events to a region, aggregate stats within regions, operator summaries per region, and tree highlighting.</td>
+  <td><span class="pri pri-med">Medium</span> <span class="effort">S</span></td>
+  <td><span class="tag tag-feat">Enhancement</span></td>
+  <td class="solution-cell">In <code>Trace2Tree/trace_to_tree.py</code>, detect <code>cat == "user_annotation"</code> or <code>cat == "python_function"</code> events from <code>record_function</code>. Add <code>get_df_by_region(region_name)</code> to <code>TreePerfAnalyzer</code> that scopes the unified perf table to the subtree under a named region.</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr data-tags="feat">
+  <td class="id-cell"><a href="https://github.com/AMD-AGI/TraceLens/issues/103" target="_blank">#103</a></td>
+  <td class="title-cell">TL Jarvis: Fully Automated Agent for Perf &amp; Opt</td>
+  <td class="desc-cell">End-to-end AI agent that: (1) adds profiling to a repo, (2) runs TraceLens perf analysis, (3) performs event replay and tuning on live GPU, (4) files minimal repro tickets automatically. 6-month roadmap item.</td>
+  <td><span class="pri pri-low">Low</span> <span class="effort">XL</span></td>
+  <td><span class="tag tag-feat">Major Feature</span></td>
+  <td class="solution-cell">Requires LLM agent scaffold using TraceLens Python API as tools. Start with a <code>TraceLensAgent</code> class wrapping <code>TreePerfAnalyzer</code> and <code>EventReplayer</code>. Phase 1: automated report summarization. Phase 2: replay-based tuning loop.</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr data-tags="feat">
+  <td class="id-cell"><a href="https://github.com/AMD-AGI/TraceLens/issues/104" target="_blank">#104</a></td>
+  <td class="title-cell">p2p NCCL support</td>
+  <td class="desc-cell">Add bus bandwidth estimation for point-to-point NCCL kernels (send/recv), which are currently not covered by <code>NcclAnalyser</code>. These appear in pipeline parallelism workloads.</td>
+  <td><span class="pri pri-med">Medium</span> <span class="effort">S</span></td>
+  <td><span class="tag tag-feat">Enhancement</span></td>
+  <td class="solution-cell">In <code>NcclAnalyser/nccl_analyser.py</code>, extend <code>is_communication_string()</code> in <code>util.py</code> to detect p2p patterns. Add bus bandwidth formula for send/recv: <code>msg_bytes / duration</code>. Expose in <code>build_df_long()</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr data-tags="feat">
+  <td class="id-cell"><a href="https://github.com/AMD-AGI/TraceLens/issues/113" target="_blank">#113</a></td>
+  <td class="title-cell">Pass event replay to HW counter profiling</td>
+  <td class="desc-cell">After replaying an op via <code>EventReplayer</code>, pass the replayed kernel through <code>rocprof-compute</code> to collect hardware performance counters (cache utilization, wavefront occupancy, memory bandwidth, etc.).</td>
+  <td><span class="pri pri-low">Low</span> <span class="effort">L</span></td>
+  <td><span class="tag tag-feat">Enhancement</span></td>
+  <td class="solution-cell">In <code>EventReplay/event_replay.py</code>, add optional <code>hw_profile=True</code> flag to <code>replay()</code>. Wrap the replayed op execution in a <code>subprocess</code> call to <code>rocprof-compute</code>. Parse and return the HW counter CSV alongside the timing result.</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr data-tags="feat">
+  <td class="id-cell"><a href="https://github.com/AMD-AGI/TraceLens/issues/114" target="_blank">#114</a></td>
+  <td class="title-cell">Perf projection</td>
+  <td class="desc-cell">Project the end-to-end performance impact of improving a specific op. An op on the non-critical path may not improve e2e even if 2× faster. Requires modeling op dependencies and the execution critical path.</td>
+  <td><span class="pri pri-low">Low</span> <span class="effort">XL</span></td>
+  <td><span class="tag tag-feat">Major Feature</span></td>
+  <td class="solution-cell">Depends on critical path analysis (#306). Once the critical path DAG is available, implement an Amdahl-style projection: for each op, compute its fraction on the critical path and the e2e speedup from a hypothetical improvement ratio. New module <code>PerfProjection/</code>.</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr data-tags="feat">
+  <td class="id-cell"><a href="https://github.com/AMD-AGI/TraceLens/issues/115" target="_blank">#115</a></td>
+  <td class="title-cell">Input arch details from user for roofline</td>
+  <td class="desc-cell">Allow users to pass a simple dict of hardware specs (peak TFLOPS, peak bandwidth) directly to <code>TreePerfAnalyzer.from_file()</code> instead of requiring a predefined architecture JSON file.</td>
+  <td><span class="pri pri-med">Medium</span> <span class="effort">M</span></td>
+  <td><span class="tag tag-feat">Enhancement</span></td>
+  <td class="solution-cell">In <code>TreePerf/tree_perf.py</code>, modify <code>from_file(arch=...)</code> to accept either a string (existing preset name/path) or a dict like <code>{'peak_perf': 1307e12, 'peak_bw': 5.3e12}</code>. Add dict-to-arch-object conversion in the factory method.</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr data-tags="feat">
+  <td class="id-cell"><a href="https://github.com/AMD-AGI/TraceLens/issues/124" target="_blank">#124</a></td>
+  <td class="title-cell">Fwd/bwd pass breakdown for kernel launchers</td>
+  <td class="desc-cell"><code>get_df_kernel_launchers()</code> does not indicate whether each launcher belongs to the forward or backward pass. Users need a <code>pass_type</code> column to split forward vs backward analysis.</td>
+  <td><span class="pri pri-med">Medium</span> <span class="effort">S</span></td>
+  <td><span class="tag tag-feat">Enhancement</span></td>
+  <td class="solution-cell">In <code>TreePerf/tree_perf.py</code>, traverse each launcher's ancestors looking for backward-pass markers (autograd function nodes, nodes linked via <code>link_all_fwd_bwd_events()</code>). Add <code>pass_type: 'forward' | 'backward' | 'unknown'</code> column to the returned DataFrame.</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr data-tags="feat">
+  <td class="id-cell"><a href="https://github.com/AMD-AGI/TraceLens/issues/128" target="_blank">#128</a></td>
+  <td class="title-cell">Calculate TFLOPS and GB/s in node replay</td>
+  <td class="desc-cell">After replaying an op via <code>EventReplayer</code>, compute TFLOPS/s and TB/s from the measured execution time and the perf model's FLOPs/bytes values. Enables comparison of microbenchmark throughput vs workload throughput.</td>
+  <td><span class="pri pri-low">Low</span> <span class="effort">S</span></td>
+  <td><span class="tag tag-feat">Enhancement</span></td>
+  <td class="solution-cell">In <code>EventReplay/event_replay.py</code>, after <code>benchmark_func()</code> returns the median time, look up the event's perf model via <code>op_to_perf_model_class_map</code>, call <code>.flops()</code> and <code>.bytes()</code>, and append <code>tflops_s</code> and <code>tb_s</code> columns to the replay output.</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr data-tags="perf">
+  <td class="id-cell"><a href="https://github.com/AMD-AGI/TraceLens/issues/165" target="_blank">#165</a></td>
+  <td class="title-cell">Add dtype detail for FP8 TEv1 GEMM</td>
+  <td class="desc-cell">FP8 GEMMs have 4 dtype combinations (e4m3/e5m2 × e4m3/e5m2). Currently TraceLens doesn't parse the exact FP8 dtypes from <code>Concrete Inputs</code> indices 3 and 8 of <code>tex_ts_te_gemm_ts</code>. The dtype integer codes map to a known dict.</td>
+  <td><span class="pri pri-med">Medium</span> <span class="effort">S</span></td>
+  <td><span class="tag tag-perf">Perf Model</span></td>
+  <td class="solution-cell">In <code>PerfModel/perf_model.py</code> class <code>tex_ts_te_gemm_ts</code>, parse indices 3 and 8 of <code>Concrete Inputs</code> with the int-to-dtype mapping from TransformerEngine's <code>common.h</code>. Expose <code>dtype_a</code> and <code>dtype_b</code> as output columns in the unified perf table.</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr data-tags="feat">
+  <td class="id-cell"><a href="https://github.com/AMD-AGI/TraceLens/issues/171" target="_blank">#171</a></td>
+  <td class="title-cell">Align kernel launchers and perf model ops</td>
+  <td class="desc-cell">Kernel launchers show <code>aten::miopen_convolution</code>, <code>aten::cudnn_convolution</code>, <code>aten::native_convolution</code> as distinct. But the perf model treats all as <code>aten::convolution</code>. These two views need alignment so analysis is consistent.</td>
+  <td><span class="pri pri-med">Medium</span> <span class="effort">M</span></td>
+  <td><span class="tag tag-refactor">Refactor</span></td>
+  <td class="solution-cell">In <code>PerfModel/torch_op_mapping.py</code>, add alias entries: map <code>aten::miopen_convolution</code>, <code>aten::cudnn_convolution</code>, etc. all to the same <code>aten_conv</code> class. In <code>get_df_kernel_launchers()</code>, optionally normalize op names using the same alias table.</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr data-tags="bug">
+  <td class="id-cell"><a href="https://github.com/AMD-AGI/TraceLens/issues/185" target="_blank">#185</a></td>
+  <td class="title-cell">Make input strides optional in perf model</td>
+  <td class="desc-cell">Some traces omit tensor stride information from <code>Concrete Inputs</code>. The perf model currently crashes when strides are missing instead of gracefully handling the absence.</td>
+  <td><span class="pri pri-high">High</span> <span class="effort">S</span></td>
+  <td><span class="tag tag-bug">Bug</span></td>
+  <td class="solution-cell">In <code>PerfModel/perf_model.py</code> base class input parsers, wrap stride extraction in a try/except or add a <code>None</code> check. Default to assuming contiguous layout (row-major strides) when strides are absent. Add regression test with a stride-less fixture.</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr data-tags="feat">
+  <td class="id-cell"><a href="https://github.com/AMD-AGI/TraceLens/issues/187" target="_blank">#187</a></td>
+  <td class="title-cell">Expose roofline plotting as importable Python API</td>
+  <td class="desc-cell">Currently roofline plotting only works via the CLI in <code>examples/custom_workflows/roofline_analyzer/</code>. Users want to call a Python function directly on a <code>TreePerfAnalyzer</code> result — no intermediate Excel file required.</td>
+  <td><span class="pri pri-med">Medium</span> <span class="effort">M</span></td>
